---

Load the kd-system skill. Read the INTENT KD at {intent_kd}. Read SPEC KDs, PLAN KDs, and IMPL KDs from KD PATHS. Review the implementation AND run the security audit per the scope above. Produce a REVIEW KD (review findings + audit section) at {result_kd} using the naming convention: knowledge/review-<name>-<session_id>-gen{generation}.md

Verdict Rules (binding):
- Write the verdict into the review KD frontmatter as a single `verdict: PASS | FAIL` field — it is the machine source protocol-gate reads at VERIFY.
- `MISSING` (absent or invalid verdict) blocks VERIFY — never treated as PASS.
- `PASS` advances only when the review KD is newer than the newest impl KD (fresh PASS after the last fix); a stale PASS blocks pending re-review.
- `FAIL` regresses VERIFY→SWARM and reopens the checked-off milestone rows named in the frontmatter `reopen_target` field — a scalar (`reopen_target: M3`) or a list (`reopen_target: [M3, M7]`). That field selects the reopened rows; milestone-shaped tokens in the findings, the traceability matrix or a References list stay provenance.
- A `reopen_target` that is absent, empty, malformed, declared twice, or names a row the registry lacks is refused with `REOPEN_TARGET_INVALID` plus its reason (`no-reopen-target`, `invalid-reopen-target`, `ambiguous-target`, `unresolvable-reopen-target` for an unknown row) — the gate blocks, regresses nothing and reopens nothing; re-issue the review with a usable field.
- To escalate a design-level failure instead of requesting a fix, issue `FAIL` with no `reopen_target` field and add a level-2 section titled `Escalation` with at least one non-empty line before the next level-2 heading — the gate blocks as `REOPEN_TARGET_INVALID reason=no-reopen-target`, regresses nothing and reopens nothing.
